# The contracts and the typed branches of the filtered structural recursion
# nat_fold_filtered of parallel_types. Each lemma holds for every base and
# every step: nat_fold_filtered filters the base, the recursive result
# handed to the step and the step's output by nat_type, so no lemma here
# asks anything of the step. A fold whose step HM rejects gets the output
# type all the same, as nat_fold_filtered (successor zero) true does. The
# lemmas are sound, and they are kept out of the lemma set of HM. The lemmas
# on list_fold_filtered are in filtered_recursion_lists and
# filtered_recursion_applied, so that every lemma set is a union of whole
# modules: a configuration enables these four without them.
#
# A typed branch adds to a term a smaller alternative, A = A + B with B ≤ A,
# an equation that holds up to ≃_O, so adding B changes the meaning of no
# term in any context, and dropping A at
# compile time only loses answers.
#
# Every lemma here is a theorem of λ-lattice-unit-η (CONTRIBUTING.md,
# "Terms"); each declaration cites its paper proof. The
# Lean module ParallelTypesTheorems (gezi/lean) derives them. None uses
# induction. This module declares no define: it uses compose (prelude),
# filter_nat, nat_fold and nat_fold_filtered (parallel_types), with which it
# is compiled.

# The contracts of structural recursion with filters, for every base and
# every step: every output path of nat_fold_filtered ends with filter_nat.
